cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyunbil (동현빌): an educational village-outbreak laboratory on a real contact network, controlled through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "0.38.0"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/raspberry-kim/donghyun-lab3"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab3/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunbil is a browser-based, JavaScript educational tool for exploring
  infectious disease transmission, vaccination and isolation policies. It
  simulates hypothetical outbreaks (measles, pertussis, influenza) on the
  publicly released Haslemere contact data (469 participants, 3 days,
  5-minute resolution), with all interventions specified only through the
  esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang. It is a teaching model, not a
  forecasting or policy-decision tool.
keywords:
  - epidemiology education
  - infectious disease modelling
  - vaccination
  - contact network
  - citizen science data
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
